# Cloudflare Pages rewrites.
#
# We need to:
#   1. Serve static SEO assets (robots.txt, sitemap.xml, og-default.png,
#      rss.xml, feed.xml, atom.xml) at their real paths, NOT through
#      the SPA fallback. Otherwise search crawlers and feed readers
#      see "index.html" for /sitemap.xml and /rss.xml — totally broken.
#   2. Keep the SPA fallback for everything else (Flutter web).
#
# Order matters: more-specific rules win, so the static assets are
# listed before the catch-all.

# Real SEO / feed / brand assets — serve the files we shipped in /web/.
/robots.txt     /robots.txt    200
/sitemap.xml    /sitemap.xml   200
/og-default.png /og-default.png 200
/twitter-card.png /twitter-card.png 200
/rss.xml        /rss.xml       200
/feed.xml       /feed.xml      200
/atom.xml       /atom.xml      200
/favicon.svg    /favicon.svg   200
/favicon-16.png /favicon-16.png 200
/favicon-32.png /favicon-32.png 200
/favicon-48.png /favicon-48.png 200
/apple-touch-icon.png /apple-touch-icon.png 200
/icon-192.png   /icon-192.png   200
/icon-512.png   /icon-512.png   200
/icon-maskable-192.png /icon-maskable-192.png 200
/icon-maskable-512.png /icon-maskable-512.png 200
# Google Search Console verification file. Body is
# `google-site-verification: googleBguSVNY65bi...html` (a single
# line, the standard Google file-format token). Belt-and-suspenders
# with the <meta> tag in index.html.
/googleBguSVNY65bi-pvRVGT8KqpBUnwMutY6BWAqkUBrKTR0.html /googleBguSVNY65bi-pvRVGT8KqpBUnwMutY6BWAqkUBrKTR0.html 200

# iOS Universal Links + Android App Links. The .well-known/
# directory is where the OS fetches these from, but Flutter's
# build process strips "dotfiles" by default, so the static
# files in /web/.well-known/ need to be served via a redirect
# to bypass the SPA fallback. The file extensions are
# .json-less for the iOS one (must be served as
# application/json — see _headers) and .json for Android.
#
# The bundle ID / SHA-256 / team ID are placeholders. Update
# them when the iOS + Android apps ship — see the README at
# /web/.well-known/README.md.
/.well-known/apple-app-site-association /.well-known/apple-app-site-association 200
/.well-known/assetlinks.json             /.well-known/assetlinks.json             200

# SPA fallback — every unknown path returns index.html so GoRouter
# can take over on the client. Required with PathUrlStrategy so
# /blog, /tools/merge, /pricing etc. all resolve correctly.
/*    /index.html   200
